@page "/datagrid-semantic-search"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor DataGrid <strong>Semantic Search</strong>
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Search a Blazor DataGrid by meaning instead of exact words. "Something to drink" finds the beverages and "Italian cheese" finds Gorgonzola and Mozzarella, even though none of the rows contain those words.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="DataGrid" Example="DataGridSemanticSearch">
    <DataGridSemanticSearch />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mt-8">
    Every row is turned into a short description and embedded once with the <code>IEmbeddingGenerator</code> from <code>IAIChatService.GetEmbeddingGenerator()</code> - the one registered in the
    service collection or the built-in <code>OpenAICompatibleEmbeddingGenerator</code> configured by <code>AIChatServiceOptions.EmbeddingsModel</code> and <code>EmbeddingsEndpoint</code>.
    The query is embedded the same way and the rows are ranked by cosine similarity with <code>TensorPrimitives.CosineSimilarity</code>; the top matches are shown with their score.
    For large data sets store the vectors next to the rows, or in a vector database, instead of computing them on the page.
</RadzenText>
